tip: | Look at the lamp. | A post two pixels wide is hard to shade, so it gets one light column and one dark one. That is all a thin form needs.
tip: 2 | Parts, one color each. | Base, post, collar, lantern, cap. At this stage it should already read as a street lamp, with nothing but its silhouette.
tip: 4 | Glow is a pattern, not a blend. | Pixels here are opaque, so light cannot fade. A checker near the lantern, then sparser dots, and the eye mixes them with the dusk behind.
tip: | Try it. | Put a dark layer behind the lamp and the glow comes up. Dither is the tool that made it. | dither
